#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise"
msgstr "Ejercicio"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "See also"
msgstr "Ver también"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr "<a cbot>Programación</a>, <a cbot|type>tipos</a> y <a cbot|category>categorías</a>."

#. type: Title-text
#: ../scene.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Radar and traps 1"
msgstr "Radar y trampas 1"

#. type: Resume-text
#: ../scene.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use your radar to look for various items, but watch out for the mines."
msgstr "Usa tu radar para buscar varios objetos, pero cuidado con las minas."

#. type: ScriptName-text
#: ../scene.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Traps"
msgstr "Trampas"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruct the bot to find all the <a object|waypoint>blue crosses</a> on the ground, but do not get too close to the <a object|mine>mines</a>. When the bot passes over a cross, it disappears. Here is the general principle:"
msgstr "Instruye al bot para que encuentre todas las <a object|waypoint>cruces azules</a> en el suelo, pero no te acerques demasiado a las <a object|mine>minas</a>. Cuando el bot pasa sobre una cruz, desaparece. Aquí está el principio general:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tRepeat forever:"
msgstr "\tRepetir para siempre:"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Look for a mine"
msgstr "Busca una mina"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a mine has been found, calculate the opposite direction"
msgstr "Si se ha encontrado una mina, calcula la dirección opuesta"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Look for a cross"
msgstr "Busca una cruz"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "If nothing has been found, stop the program"
msgstr "Si no se ha encontrado nada, detén el programa"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the direction of the cross"
msgstr "Calcula la dirección de la cruz"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the mean value of the two directions"
msgstr "Calcula el valor medio de las dos direcciones"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the motor speeds in order to head towards the mean direction"
msgstr "Establece las velocidades del motor para ir en la dirección media"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "The instruction <code>radar</code>"
msgstr "La instrucción <code>radar</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to detect a mine with the <code><a cbot|radar>radar</a></code>, we recommend the following parameters:\n"
"<c/><s/>\tradar(Mine, 0, 180, 0, 5);<n/>\n"
"With the opening angle of 180 degrees, mines that are behind the bot will not be found. Mines that are at more than 5 meters are also ignored."
msgstr ""
"Para detectar una mina con el <code><a cbot|radar>radar</a></code>, recomendamos los siguientes parámetros:\n"
"<c/><s/>\tradar(Mine, 0, 180, 0, 5);<n/>\n"
"Con el ángulo de apertura de 180 grados, las minas que están detrás del bot no se encontrarán. Las minas que están a más de 5 metros también se ignoran."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to find a blue cross, simply write:\n"
"<c/><s/>\tradar(WayPoint);<n/>\n"
"Blue crosses will be found everywhere."
msgstr ""
"Para encontrar una cruz azul, simplemente escribe:\n"
"<c/><s/>\tradar(WayPoint);<n/>\n"
"Las cruces azules se encontrarán por todas partes."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to calculate a direction, use <code><a cbot|direct>direction</a></code>.\n"
"In order to set the motor speeds, use <code><a cbot|motor>motor</a></code>."
msgstr ""
"Para calcular una dirección, usa <code><a cbot|direct>direction</a></code>.\n"
"Para establecer las velocidades del motor, usa <code><a cbot|motor>motor</a></code>."
